From bb091b5a18d89fcc9c9a6a2911eae8d79ab24b15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:26:02 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Frame rate ceiling 500: presets 300, 360 and 480

- The frame rate setting's top is 500 (was 240): presets 300, 360 and 480 join the list, Custom takes 61-500 and
  Monitor follows displays up to 500 Hz, so fast monitors run the game natively at their own rate.
- Tests: the new presets, the 500 clamp, a 360 Hz monitor kept at 360 and a 600 Hz one clamped.

Verified: unit tests (the settings suites pass); a desktop run on the GPU path at GA2_FPS=360 on a 360 Hz display:
the governor climbs to 300 and 360 where there is headroom (370-390 iterations/s) and steps down in heavier scenes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ga2_framepace.h |  4 ++--
 ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ga2_options.h   |  8 ++++----
 ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ga2_framepace.cpp       |  8 ++++----
 ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ga2_settings.cpp        |  2 +-
 ps2xTest/src/ga2_settings_tests.cpp         | 16 +++++++++-------
 5 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

